{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '261,460p' /Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/SKILL.md\"","aggregated_output":"task-board m 'unlink(TASK-260218-def456, blocked_by=TASK-260218-abc123)'                    # remove dependency\ntask-board m 'check_item(TASK-260218-abc123, item=1)'                                       # check checklist item\ntask-board m 'add_checklist_item(TASK-260218-abc123, text=\"Write tests\")'                   # add checklist item\ntask-board m 'set_notes(TASK-260218-abc123, text=\"Progress update\")'                        # append notes\ntask-board m 'set_notes(TASK-260218-abc123, text=\"Full replacement\", set=true)'             # replace notes\ntask-board m 'set_parent(TASK-260218-abc123, parent=STORY-260218-def456)'                   # move to new parent\ntask-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260218-abc123, name=TASK-260218-abc123_design.md, content=\"...\", type=precondition, description=\"Architecture design\")'  # create resource\ntask-board m 'update_resource(TASK-260218-abc123, name=TASK-260218-abc123_design.md, content=\"revised\", type=precondition, description=\"Architecture design v2\")'  # replace resource\ntask-board m --dry-run 'delete(TASK-260218-abc123)'                                         # preview destructive op\ntask-board m --confirm 'delete(TASK-260218-abc123)'                                         # execute destructive op\n\n# Batching (semicolons)\ntask-board m 'assign(TASK-260218-abc123, agent=claude-opus); set_status(TASK-260218-abc123, status=development)'\n\n# Spawn tracked background runs (--role, --background, and --model are REQUIRED; Codex/Qwen also require --reasoning-effort)\ntask-board spawn TASK-260218-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max\ntask-board spawn TASK-260218-abc123 --role researcher --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max\ntask-board spawn TASK-260218-abc123 --role reviewer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max\ntask-board spawn TASK-260218-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-sol --reasoning-effort max --instruction impl-guide.md\ntask-board spawn TASK-260218-abc123 --role developer --background --agent claude --model claude-opus-4-8 --budget 5.0\ntask-board spawn TASK-260218-abc123 --role developer --background --agent qwen --model qwen3.7-plus --reasoning-effort xhigh\ntask-board spawn TASK-260218-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-terra --reasoning-effort max\ntask-board spawn TASK-260218-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.6-luna --reasoning-effort max\ntask-board spawn TASK-260218-abc123 --role developer --background --agent codex --model gpt-5.3-codex-spark --reasoning-effort xhigh\ntask-board spawn status RUN-260320-abc123                                            # inspect tracked run state\ntask-board spawn wait RUN-260320-abc123                                              # block on tracked run state after RUN exists\ntask-board spawn events RUN-260320-abc123                                            # replay durable run events (supports --cursor/--follow)\ntask-board spawn watch RUN-260320-abc123                                             # follow durable run-event notifications\n\n# Auth (always local, never sent to server)\ntask-board login sampleuser tb_4lc6...                                        # store token in Keychain and select active user outside repo config\ntask-board login admin tb_UJTW... --remote https://board.example.com          # explicit remote bootstrap\ntask-board logout                                                              # remove selected user's token\ntask-board whoami                                                              # show remote URL + active user + token status\ntask-board switch-user admin                                                   # switch active user without touching versioned config\ntask-board q 'whoami()'                                                        # whoami via query DSL\ntask-board q 'project_config()'                                                # mode, board source, and effective spawn policy\ntask-board m 'login(user=sampleuser, token=tb_xxx)'                           # login via mutation DSL\ntask-board m 'switch_user(user=admin)'                                         # switch via mutation DSL\n\n# CLI utilities\ntask-board grep \"AudioRecorder\"                            # full-text search across board files (local only)\ntask-board validate                                        # check board structure (local only)\ntask-board repair-links                                    # list unsupported stored container links (local, read-only)\ntask-board repair-links STORY-260218-abc123 --confirm      # remove selected suspicious links\ntask-board tui                                             # interactive terminal dashboard\n```\n\n---\n\n## Task Board Structure\n\n### Hierarchy\n\n```\nEpic → Story → Task/Bug\n```\n\n- **Epic** = large feature / module\n- **Story** = specific functionality within epic\n- **Task** = atomic unit of work\n- **Bug** = defect tracked within a story\n\n### Naming Convention\n\n**Distributed IDs** — each element gets a unique ID based on date + random hash.\n\n```\nEPIC-260203-a1b2c3_recording/\n  STORY-260203-d4e5f6_audio-capture/\n    TASK-260203-g7h8i9_audiorecorder-interface/\n    TASK-260203-j0k1l2_implementation/\n    BUG-260203-m3n4o5_some-bug/\n```\n\nFormat: `{TYPE}-{YYMMDD}-{hash}_{kebab-case-name}`\n- `EPIC-YYMMDD-xxxxxx_name`\n- `STORY-YYMMDD-xxxxxx_name`\n- `TASK-YYMMDD-xxxxxx_name`\n- `BUG-YYMMDD-xxxxxx_name`\n\nWhere:\n- `YYMMDD` — creation date (year, month, day)\n- `xxxxxx` — 6-character base36 hash (collision-resistant)\n\nIDs are globally unique and work in parallel environments (no counter conflicts).\n\n### Directory Layout\n\n```\n.task-board/\n├── .resources/                   # Flat resource storage (managed by CLI)\n│   ├── TASK-260203-g7h8i9/       # Resources keyed by element ID\n│   │   ├── design.md             # Precondition: input for the task\n│   │   └── results.md            # Outcome: work product\n│   └── STORY-260203-d4e5f6/\n│       └── research.md\n├── EPIC-260203-a1b2c3_recording/\n│   ├── README.md                 # Epic description, scope, AC\n│   ├── progress.md               # Status, blockedBy, checklist, notes, resource refs\n│   ├── STORY-260203-d4e5f6_audio-capture/\n│   │   ├── README.md\n│   │   ├── progress.md\n│   │   ├── TASK-260203-g7h8i9_interface/\n│   │   │   ├── README.md\n│   │   │   └── progress.md\n│   │   ├── TASK-260203-j0k1l2_implementation/\n│   │   │   ├── README.md\n│   │   │   └── progress.md\n│   │   └── BUG-260203-m3n4o5_crash-on-start/\n│   │       ├── README.md\n│   │       └── progress.md\n│   └── STORY-260203-p6q7r8_amplitude/\n│       └── ...\n└── EPIC-260203-s9t0u1_storage/\n    └── ...\n```\n\nNo `system.md` needed — IDs are self-contained and don't require global counters.\n\n---\n\n## Statuses\n\n9 statuses: `backlog` → `analysis` → `to-dev` → `development` → `to-review` → `reviewing` → `done`. Plus `closed` and `blocked`.\n\nBefore a newly created Task/Bug enters `development`, set its estimate with\n`set_estimate(ID, estimate=estimated, scale=fibonacci, number=N)`. The start\ntransition returns a typed estimate-required error while the explicit value is\n`notEstimated`. Legacy Task/Bug files that have no Estimate section are\ngrandfathered and remain startable.\n\n`done` is accepted leaf work or computed container completion; `closed` is an\nexplicit administrative disposition. A story or epic may remain `closed` only\nwhile every direct and transitive descendant is `done` or `closed`.\n\nFor full status flow, auto-promotion/reopen, blocked vs is_blocked — see [`references/statuses.md`](references/statuses.md).\n\n---\n\n## File Formats\n\nEach element directory contains two files:\n- **README.md** — static description (what the element is, scope, acceptance criteria). Does not change during execution.\n- **progress.md** — dynamic lifecycle journal (status, Task/Bug estimate, assignment, timestamps, dependencies, checklist, notes). Updated throughout execution.\n\nBoth files use source-aware, injection-safe Markdown persistence. Unchanged\nbytes and custom sections are retained during rewrites; free-text payload fields\nround-trip byte-exact. Mutation boundaries normalize identifier-like fields\n(`AssignedTo`, `BlockedBy`, `Blocks`) by trimming boundary whitespace and reject\nempty or reserved `(none)` values with a typed error. Checklist text is rejected\nonly when empty-after-trim and is otherwise persisted verbatim.\n\nTask/bug dependencies are bidirectional ground truth. Story/epic ordering is derived from the live task DAG at read time; task links never materialize container side-effect links. Explicit stored container links remain manual state, while projections expose task-derived blockers separately.\n\nFor detailed format specifications, field descriptions, and examples, see [`references/file-formats.md`](references/file-formats.md).\n\n---\n\n## Resources & Bugs\n\nResources are linked to board elements via DSL mutations. Two types:\n- **Precondition** — inputs for the task (instructions, specs, design docs). Used by `task-board spawn` to compose agent prompts.\n- **Outcome** — work products (research results, implementation notes). Persisted for other agents/tasks to consume.\n\n```bash\n# Create resource\ntask-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260218-abc123, name=TASK-260218-abc123_design.md, content=\"...\", type=precondition, description=\"Architecture design\")'\ntask-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260218-abc123, name=TASK-260218-abc123_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Research findings\")'\n\n# Replace existing resource\ntask-board m 'update_resource(TASK-260218-abc123, name=TASK-260218-abc123_results.md, content=\"revised findings\", type=outcome, description=\"Research findings v2\")'\n\n# Delete resource\ntask-board m --confirm 'delete_resource(TASK-260218-abc123, name=TASK-260218-abc123_design.md)'\n```\n\nResources are stored flat in `.task-board/.resources/<elementID>/` and referenced from `progress.md`. Bugs live inside stories alongside tasks.\n\nFor resource workflow and bug tracking — see [`references/resources-and-bugs.md`](references/resources-and-bugs.md).\n\n---\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Full Development Cycle (MANDATORY)\n\nWhen the user asks to build/implement something, the agent MUST follow this end-to-end flow:\n\n#### Spec\n- Specs live in the `.spec/` directory (one or more `.md` files), not in a single `SPEC.md`\n- Create `.spec/` if it doesn't exist; add focused spec files per topic/feature (e.g. `.spec/auth.md`, `.spec/api.md`)\n- Clarify requirements with the user if anything is ambiguous\n- `.spec/` is the source of truth — all work traces back to it\n\n#### Plan on the Board\n- Create epics and stories: `task-board m 'create(type=epic, name=..., description=\"...\")'`\n- Refine each element: query with `task-board q 'get(ID) { full }'`, clarify gaps, update via `task-board m 'set_details(ID, description=\"...\")'`\n- Perform spec-to-board decomposition inline as the Orchestrator; do not create a meta-task or spawn `solution-architect` merely to lay out a settled spec\n- No element should have placeholder text — description and AC must be complete and unambiguous\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
