nscope:curator-spec manager-profile prose, CLI contracts, lifecycle state machine, stable diagnostics, and normative command examples. Reuse the accepted go-v1 trusted toolchain/build session without changing its schema-6 meaning.\nac:The profile fixes supported transports and canonical identity, exact init/fetch/ref flows, SSH isolation, local-substitution admission, pack/index and cat-file grammar, commit/tag/tree/blob recomputation, complete-object and all-blob LFS proof, audit ordering, cache and receipt keys, marker currentness, rollback, repair and GC roots; tagged declarations always exact-fetch the tag as the sole path; syntax-only offline warning and install/audit failure are unambiguous; no repository-controlled hooks, helpers, filters, argv, env, output, credentials, signing, or lazy network reads remain possible; profile examples and validation pass.\nblockedBy:[\"TASK-260728-1a52au\",\"TASK-260728-17sclp\"]\nblocks:[\"TASK-260728-3b8qym\"]\nderivedBlockedBy:[]\nderivedBlocks:[]\nchecklist:[{\"text\":\"Validate exact Git, offline, audit, cache, transaction, status, repair, and GC examples\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"Document stable typed failures and package-controlled behavior rejections\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"Docs updated and consistent with current code\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"No discrepancies between code and description\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"Result linked as a new task-scoped outcome resource\",\"done\":false},{\"text\":\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\",\"done\":false}]\nnotes:Execution directive (2026-07-28): Target /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator-spec. Create isolated /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-wy3dsw/curator-spec-worktree from pinned HEAD 57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730 and seed the complete accepted uncommitted state from /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-17sclp/curator-spec-worktree byte-for-byte, excluding .git, .temp, caches and task build artifacts. Do not mutate prior/source worktrees; no commit or staging. Treat architecture-v6, accepted Core/Decision 0005, and accepted 42-schema/400-vector wire corpus as binding and frozen. Implement only the exact rc.5 manager profile/CLI/lifecycle contract: trusted Git release/session and clean environment; private init and exact fetch/ref flows; HTTPS and fixed SSH wrapper; local files-ref repository admission; config/ref/pack/index/cat-file and commit/tag/tree/blob grammar; complete graph/LFS/submodule/link/special-file rejection; snapshot materialization and independent audit/policy ordering; protected snapshot/artifact identities and cache behavior; dry-run/offline semantics; mixed receipt/marker planning; manager-derived build/staging/shim/PATH; transaction/rollback/recovery; read-only status, repair, deduplication and GC; stable diagnostics; credential and signer fail-closed boundaries. Preserve go-v1/rc.4 profile behavior and wire bytes. Exact normative argv/environments, state transitions, limits, error mapping, CLI output/exit semantics and examples belong here; schemas, shared executable conformance fixtures, manager implementations, release metadata and future drivers do not. Inspect existing profile/CLI conventions, keep docs English, add focused examples/checks where appropriate, run link/schema/docs and full validation, accepted-baseline comparisons, diff/no-stage/no-commit checks, attach a task-scoped outcome mapping architecture sections to text and evidence, and route to to-review.\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\nspawn queued: [implementer] doc-writer (codex) (run=RUN-260727-fef777, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] doc-writer (codex) (run=RUN-260727-fef