.md:217:- `build_repository_ref_moved`;\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:218:- `build_repository_unverified_offline`;\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:219:- `build_repository_incomplete_source`;\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:220:- `build_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid`;\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:221:- `build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported`;\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:222:- `build_repository_local_gitfile_unsupported`;\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:223:- `build_repository_local_bare_unsupported`;\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:224:- `build_repository_local_linked_worktree_unsupported`;\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:225:- `build_repository_local_layout_unsafe`;\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:226:- `build_repository_local_format_unsupported`; and\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:227:- `build_repository_local_object_format_unsupported`.\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:230:credential-policy, audit, protected-boundary, receipt, marker, artifact,\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:232:the prohibited downstream action. The manager profile defines their CLI\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:234:cache hit, audit success, source unavailability, or generic fallback.\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:238:- Reusing or widening `go-v1` was rejected because it would change the frozen\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:239:  rc.4 source, receipt, marker, and audit contract.\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:249:- Receipt-only provenance and permission repair/adoption were rejected because\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:252:  form loses a required half of the cache and audit identity.\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:259:This decision adds only the schema-7/rc.5 surface. All rc.4 artifacts retain\ndecisions/0005-external-build-repositories.md:270:toolchain and transaction boundary. Remote Git data, repository configuration,\nGOVERNANCE.md:4:`github.com/relux-works/curator-spec`. The repository is the canonical source\nGOVERNANCE.md:40:and remains available for audit.\ndecisions/0003-production-registry-service.md:21:snapshot metadata, and auditor-scoped idempotency results are one serialized\ndecisions/0003-production-registry-service.md:32:- Globally scoped idempotency keys were rejected because one auditor could\ndecisions/0003-production-registry-service.md:33:  collide with another auditor's request.\ndecisions/0003-production-registry-service.md:46:The decision prevents cross-auditor idempotency denial, pagination races,\nCHANGELOG.md:46:  queries, exact artifact identity, snapshot-bound cursors, auditor-scoped\nCHANGELOG.md:60:- Scoped idempotency keys to an auditor and compared the submitted record's\nCHANGELOG.md:101:- Split normative protocol core, registry, manager profile, and conformance\nCHANGELOG.md:108:- A repository-pinned SSH signer allowlist verified by release CI for both the\ndecisions/0002-canonical-json-and-registry-trust.md:6:precision, escaping, key selection, Merkle bytes, snapshots, and offline\ndecisions/0002-canonical-json-and-registry-trust.md:45:offline bundle from bootstrapping its own trust anchor. Implementations still\ncli/curator.md:20:| `curator install [target] [--all] [--dry-run] [--strict-tags] [--audit [advisory\\|strict]]` | Apply the manager lifecycle |\ncli/curator.md:30:| `curator audit [target] [--all] [--global] [--json]` | Run source audit |\ncli/curator.md:31:| `curator audit --allow <hash> --reason <text>` | Create an operator pin |\ncli/curator.md:32:| `curator audit --publish <record> --registry <url>` | Publish an auditor-signed record |\ncli/curator.md:33:| `curator gc` | Collect unreferenced machine state |\ncli/curator.md:40:`bootstrap --if-missing` is intended for repository bootstrap commands. It\ncli/curator.md:46:fetches every repository below `skills_root`. `upgrade --all` deduplicates\ncli/curator.md:95:Organizations normally install enforced source, audit, and registry policy\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
