{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} '\"' /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-wy3dsw/architecture-v6.md\"","aggregated_output":"1:# External build repositories: architecture decision and threat model, revision 6\n10:## 1. Decision summary\n36:### 1.1 Change required by the fifth independent review\n55:### 1.2 Justified gap and self-verification\n69:## 2. Manifest schema 7 and compatibility\n117:## 3. Exact Git source grammar and immutable lock\n119:### 3.1 Canonical network identity\n136:### 3.2 Safe tag and development-ref grammar\n161:### 3.3 Lock and optional tag assertion\n180:## 4. Repository descriptor and output boundary\n215:## 5. Declared and effective source identity\n217:### 5.1 Source states\n251:### 5.2 Skillfile.dev schema 2\n283:## 6. Closed Git child and object boundary\n285:### 6.1 Trusted distribution, process graph, and clean environment\n361:### 6.2 Exact private repository initialization\n397:### 6.3 Exact network fetch and ref flows\n588:### 6.4 Exact SSH wrapper and OpenSSH invocation\n720:### 6.5 Local substitution admission: deliberately narrow v1\n745:#### 6.5.1 Byte-level config admission\n788:#### 6.5.2 Files-ref parsing and selected HEAD\n813:#### 6.5.3 Exact object inventory and interoperable pack admission\n909:### 6.6 Common raw-object reader and complete-object proof\n915:#### 6.6.1 Exact `cat-file --batch` process\n994:#### 6.6.2 Manager parsing and graph proof\n1166:#### 6.6.3 Exact all-blob Git LFS rejection\n1336:## 7. Snapshot identity and audit equivalence\n1357:## 8. Receipt v2, cache identity, and mixed schema-7 builds\n1359:### 8.1 Unsubstituted external receipt input\n1433:### 8.2 Substituted external receipt input\n1490:### 8.3 Mixed command behavior\n1503:## 9. Marker v3, status, repair, deduplication, and GC\n1566:### 9.1 Snapshot and artifact keys\n1574:### 9.2 Read-only status\n1594:### 9.3 Repair\n1605:### 9.4 Garbage collection roots\n1616:## 10. Deterministic build, install, PATH, and rollback\n1645:## 11. Signing and notarization boundary\n1665:## 12. Future closed-driver rule\n1686:## 13. Threat model\n1688:### 13.1 Adversary-controlled\n1696:### 13.2 Trusted computing base\n1705:### 13.3 Required controls\n1730:## 14. Exact impact on existing board work\n1734:### 14.1 Existing curator-spec schema-6 story\n1751:### 14.2 Existing Curator implementation story\n1765:### 14.3 Existing cocoaskills implementation story\n1771:### 14.4 Existing interoperability story\n1785:## 15. Rejected alternatives\n1810:## 16. Primary-source register\n1861:## 17. Validation and independent-review checks\n1921:### 17.1 Producer verification evidence\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
