{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1001,1500p' /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/.temp/TASK-260728-wy3dsw/architecture-v6.md\"","aggregated_output":"The common **header-record grammar** is:\n\n1. An object is bounded before parsing and contains no NUL byte anywhere.\n2. Its header block uses LF only. CR is forbidden before the header/body\n   separator. The separator is the first exact `LF LF` and is required even\n   when the message is empty. A lone final header LF is not enough.\n3. A primary header line is\n   `<key> SP <value> LF`. `key` is one or more ASCII letters, digits, or `-`,\n   begins with an ASCII letter, and has no normalization. `value` is a bounded\n   byte string with no LF, CR, or NUL and may be empty only for an\n   implementation-ignored extra header.\n4. Zero or more continuation lines may follow an extra header only. Each is\n   `SP <continuation-bytes> LF`; the continuation bytes may be empty and\n   contain no LF, CR, or NUL. A continuation before the first header or after a\n   required structural header is invalid. This admits ordinary `gpgsig`,\n   `gpgsig-sha256`, and `mergetag` records without interpreting or verifying\n   their signatures.\n5. Bytes after the separator are a bounded opaque message. They may contain\n   LF, CR, non-UTF-8 bytes, and signature armor, but not NUL. Message bytes\n   never select a ref, tree, target, cache key field, credential, or process.\n\nA selected **commit** MUST match this ordered grammar:\n\n1. The first record is exactly `tree <H-hex>` with no continuation.\n2. Zero or more `parent <H-hex>` records follow contiguously, each without a\n   continuation. Their byte order is retained as object semantics; the source\n   snapshot does not traverse parent history. Repeated parent IDs are allowed\n   because they do not select compiler input.\n3. Exactly one non-empty `author <opaque-ident>` record and then exactly one\n   non-empty `committer <opaque-ident>` record follow, both without\n   continuation. Their bounded values are metadata only; the manager does not\n   reinterpret names, email, time, timezone, or signature trust.\n4. Zero or more extra records may follow the committer and may use the common\n   continuation grammar. An extra record MUST NOT use any reserved key\n   `tree`, `parent`, `author`, or `committer`; this makes a duplicate or\n   misplaced structural header invalid rather than implementation-selected.\n   Non-reserved extra keys may repeat and remain ordered opaque metadata.\n5. The exact separator follows the last record. The one tree ID is the only\n   commit field used to select snapshot content.\n\nA selected **annotated tag** MUST match this ordered grammar:\n\n1. The first record is exactly `object <H-hex>` and the second is exactly\n   `type <commit-or-tag>`, neither with a continuation.\n2. The third is exactly `tag <safe-tag-name>` with no continuation. It uses\n   section 3.2's byte grammar; the outermost tag record selected through an\n   exact tag ref MUST name that requested tag. Nested tag names are validated\n   but need not equal the outer ref.\n3. At most one non-empty `tagger <opaque-ident>` record may follow, without a\n   continuation. Early tag objects may omit it.\n4. Zero or more non-reserved extra records may then use the common\n   continuation grammar. `object`, `type`, `tag`, and `tagger` are reserved\n   and cannot reappear or occur out of order. Signed tag armor belongs to the\n   opaque message after the separator and is accepted without verification.\n5. After requesting and independently recomputing `object`, the actual\n   `cat-file` type MUST byte-equal the tag's declared `type`. `tag` continues\n   peeling; `commit` terminates it. A `tree` or `blob` target is invalid for\n   this driver. The chain contains at most 16 annotated tag objects, and no\n   full object ID may repeat. Lightweight refs point directly to a commit and\n   consume zero tag-depth slots.\n\nAny malformed commit/tag header, wrong width/case, duplicate or misplaced\nreserved header, bad/missing separator, unexpected/declared type mismatch,\ntag cycle, or tag-depth overflow fails the single stable pre-audit error:\n\n```text\nbuild_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid\n```\n\nThe manager maps the common semantic parser to this result on both network and\nlocal-store paths. A network fetch may reject corrupt bytes earlier through\nthe already required transfer fsck, but it MUST NOT turn a known object\nsemantic rejection into availability, cache-hit, or audit success.\n\nAfter a terminal commit passes:\n\n1. the manager requests its one tree ID, recomputes it, and requires actual\n   type `tree`;\n2. it parses each tree as the Git binary sequence\n   `<octal-mode> SP <name-bytes> NUL <H-byte-object-id>`, consuming the entire\n   object with no empty/duplicate name, slash, NUL, `.`/`..`, invalid UTF-8,\n   nonportable component, or platform collision;\n3. it accepts only tree mode `40000` and blob modes `100644`/`100755`; symlink\n   `120000`, gitlink `160000`, unknown modes, and mode/type mismatch fail;\n4. it reads and recomputes every reachable tree and blob, proving every\n   required object locally available without replace, graft, alternate,\n   promisor, lazy-fetch, checkout, attribute, filter, textconv, mailmap, or\n   archive transformation;\n5. it runs section 6.6.3's all-blob detector before materialization or audit;\n6. it materializes exact verified blob bytes into a frozen regular-file\n   snapshot with manager filesystem code, preserving only the executable bit\n   distinction from `100755`/`100644`.\n\nGitlinks fail before reading `.gitmodules`. Parent history, human identity,\ncommit/tag messages, signatures, and extra headers remain untrusted bounded\nmetadata and are never used as provenance.\n\nRequired cross-language semantic fixtures use UTF-8 only for compact display;\nthe parser itself is byte-oriented:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"valid-commit-with-signed-and-extra-headers\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"tree aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nparent bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\nauthor A U Thor <a@example.test> 1 +0000\\ncommitter C O Mitter <c@example.test> 2 +0000\\ngpgsig -----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\\n payload\\n -----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\\nx-curator-fixture opaque\\n\\nmessage\\r\\nbody\\n\",\n    \"expected\": \"valid\",\n    \"tree\": \"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"reject-duplicate-tree-header\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"tree aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\ntree bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\nauthor A <a@b> 1 +0000\\ncommitter C <c@d> 2 +0000\\n\\nmessage\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"reject-misordered-tree-after-parent\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"parent bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\ntree aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nauthor A <a@b> 1 +0000\\ncommitter C <c@d> 2 +0000\\n\\nmessage\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"reject-missing-header-message-separator\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"tree aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nauthor A <a@b> 1 +0000\\ncommitter C <c@d> 2 +0000\\nmessage\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"valid-signed-annotated-tag\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"tag\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"object aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\ntype commit\\ntag v1.4.0\\ntagger T Agger <t@example.test> 3 +0000\\n\\nrelease\\n-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\\nopaque\\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\\n\",\n    \"resolved_target_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"expected\": \"valid\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"reject-duplicate-object-and-type-headers\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"tag\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"object aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nobject bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\ntype commit\\ntype tag\\ntag v1.4.0\\n\\nmessage\\n\",\n    \"resolved_target_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"reject-tag-declared-target-type-mismatch\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"tag\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"object aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\ntype tag\\ntag v1.4.0\\n\\nmessage\\n\",\n    \"resolved_target_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n#### 6.6.3 Exact all-blob Git LFS rejection\n\nThe manager scans every reachable blob exactly once, regardless of path,\nextension, mode, selected build root, `.gitattributes`, or later `go list`\nselection. This happens after object-ID recomputation and before snapshot\nmaterialization, audit, cache lookup, or compiler execution. The detector never\ninvokes `git-lfs`, a filter, or the network.\n\nThe supported parser-family invariant is exactly\n`git-lfs-pointer-parser-v3.7.1`: the decoder and encoder behavior in the\nofficial Git LFS `v3.7.1` `lfs/pointer.go`, exercised by the Git LFS 3.7.1\nbinary in conformance. A different parser family requires a reviewed detector\nrevision. The protocol does not claim that the published pointer specification\nalone describes every byte form accepted by that implementation.\n\nA zero-byte blob is admitted because Git LFS encodes the empty file as empty\nGit content. Every non-empty blob of 1 through 1023 bytes is a candidate.\nExactly 1024 bytes or more is outside both the pinned decoder cutoff and this\ndetector, even if a shorter prefix looks like a pointer.\n\nFor a candidate, manager code applies this bounded compatibility algorithm:\n\n1. Remove the maximal leading and trailing sequence of Unicode White_Space\n   scalar encodings recognized by Go 1.25's `unicode.IsSpace`: ASCII HT, LF,\n   VT, FF, CR, SP; U+0085, U+00A0, U+1680, U+2000 through U+200A, U+2028,\n   U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, and U+3000. Invalid UTF-8 outside those exact\n   encodings is not trimmed. This is the cross-language definition of the\n   pinned decoder's `bytes.TrimSpace`.\n2. Split the remainder at LF. Remove one terminal CR from each line, as Go's\n   `bufio.ScanLines` does, and ignore empty lines. Embedded CR and invalid\n   UTF-8 remain ordinary bytes.\n3. Each non-empty line must contain an ASCII SP. Split at the first SP only;\n   the bytes before it are `key` and all remaining bytes are `value`.\n4. Required keys occur exactly once and in parser state order:\n   `version`, then `oid`, then `size`. While waiting for any required key, an\n   extension line may occur; no line may occur after `size`.\n5. `version` equals exactly one of:\n   `https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1`,\n   `https://hawser.github.com/spec/v1`, or\n   `http://git-media.io/v/2`.\n6. `oid` equals `sha256:` plus exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal bytes.\n7. `size` is the exact input grammar accepted by Go `strconv.ParseInt` with\n   base 10 and width 64, and its mathematical value is nonnegative. Thus\n   `+1`, `00`, and `01` are accepted noncanonical forms; a negative value,\n   overflow above signed 64-bit, whitespace, or non-decimal byte is not.\n8. An extension key begins exactly `ext-`, one ASCII digit `0` through `9`,\n   `-`, then at least one ASCII `[A-Za-z0-9_]` byte. After that first name\n   byte, every byte other than ASCII SP or LF belongs to the name; there is no\n   end-anchored name regexp. This deliberately covers lowercase/dot/dash,\n   `_`, uppercase, and names whose accepted prefix is followed by punctuation\n   such as `a!`, matching the pinned `\\Aext-\\d{1}-\\w+` behavior. The extension\n   value uses the exact OID grammar from step 6.\n9. Extension entries are first collected by their entire raw key, with a later\n   exact duplicate key replacing the earlier value as in the pinned map.\n   After collection, distinct surviving keys MUST have unique numeric\n   priorities. A repeated exact key is accepted but noncanonical; distinct\n   keys with the same priority are rejected by the pinned family and therefore\n   do not match this detector.\n10. Missing required keys, an unknown non-extension key, malformed OID/size,\n    an extension name not beginning with an ASCII word byte, a bad extension\n    value, or distinct duplicate priorities ends the match.\n\nEvery successful compatibility match is rejected, not merely strict/canonical\nmatches. Classification is diagnostic only:\n\n- `canonical` means the original blob bytes exactly equal the pinned encoder:\n  current version first; surviving extensions sorted by numeric priority and\n  emitted as their raw names; then `oid`, `size`, and one final LF, with no\n  trimming, blank line, duplicate key, or alternate spelling.\n- a non-empty pointer whose parsed size is zero is always\n  `legacy-or-noncanonical`, because the pinned encoder emits an empty blob for\n  size zero;\n- aliases, CRLF, omitted/folded endings, leading/trailing whitespace, blank\n  lines, reordered extension placement, exact duplicate keys, signed/zero-\n  padded sizes, or any other accepted bytes unequal to the encoder are also\n  `legacy-or-noncanonical`.\n\nBoth classifications fail the same stable pre-audit error:\n\n```text\nbuild_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\n```\n\nThe false-positive boundary is closed: only a non-empty blob below 1024 bytes\nthat completes all ten compatibility steps is rejected. A 1024-byte blob,\nunknown version, uppercase/bad OID, missing required key, extension beginning\nwith punctuation, or two distinct extension keys sharing a priority remains\nordinary blob content. The diagnostic may identify classification and path,\nbut MUST NOT print the pointer OID as a fetch instruction. The manager never\nhydrates from `.git/lfs`, an LFS endpoint, a filter, or local operator state.\n\nRequired cross-language fixtures:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"canonical-current-pointer\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\",\n    \"classification\": \"canonical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"canonical-extension-name-family\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\next-1-lower.dot-dash sha256:bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\next-2-_under sha256:cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc\\next-3-A_B sha256:dddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddd\\next-4-a! sha256:eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\",\n    \"classification\": \"canonical\",\n    \"git_lfs_3_7_1_strict_exit\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"accepted-crlf-blank-unsorted-and-no-terminal-lf\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"\\r\\nversion https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\r\\next-4-a! sha256:eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee\\r\\n\\r\\next-1-lower sha256:bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\r\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\r\\nsize +01\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\",\n    \"classification\": \"legacy-or-noncanonical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"accepted-exact-duplicate-key-last-value-wins\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\next-1-a sha256:bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\next-1-a sha256:cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\",\n    \"classification\": \"legacy-or-noncanonical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"distinct-duplicate-priority-is-not-accepted\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\next-1-a sha256:bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\next-1-b sha256:cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n    \"expected\": \"ordinary-blob\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"nonempty-size-zero-is-deliberately-noncanonical\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 0\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\",\n    \"classification\": \"legacy-or-noncanonical\",\n    \"git_lfs_3_7_1_strict_exit\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cutoff-1023-after-trim\",\n    \"construction\": {\n      \"prefix_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n      \"pad_byte_hex\": \"20\",\n      \"total_bytes\": 1023\n    },\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\",\n    \"classification\": \"legacy-or-noncanonical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cutoff-1024-is-ordinary\",\n    \"construction\": {\n      \"prefix_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n      \"pad_byte_hex\": \"20\",\n      \"total_bytes\": 1024\n    },\n    \"expected\": \"ordinary-blob\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"near-miss-extension-starts-with-punctuation\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\next-1-!a sha256:bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n    \"expected\": \"ordinary-blob\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"near-miss-uppercase-oid\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\noid sha256:AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA\\nsize 1\\n\",\n    \"expected\": \"ordinary-blob\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nNo audit or artifact-cache lookup begins until the object proof, LFS scan,\nmaterialization, whole-snapshot validation, and\n`curator-build-source-v1` digest succeed. Object bytes are transport input, not\nprovenance, and the object store is never agent-facing, runtime-copied, or used\ndirectly as build source.\n\n## 7. Snapshot identity and audit equivalence\n\nThe consuming skill snapshot and each effective external repository snapshot are independent untrusted audit subjects.\n\nFor every external repository selected by the active plan:\n\n1. for an unsubstituted declaration containing `tag`, complete the exact-tag\n   acquisition and terminal-lock equality check from section 6.3;\n2. validate the whole repository snapshot;\n3. compute `curator-build-source-v1` over every regular file, including `curator-build.json` and files outside the selected build root;\n4. parse the descriptor and select the target;\n5. audit the complete external snapshot under declared/effective identity, object format, effective commit, build-source digest, target, substitution state, and the verified tag assertion when applicable;\n6. apply allowlist, revocation, registry, tag-lock, and audit policy gates;\n7. only then inspect an artifact-cache candidate or start a compiler child.\n\nRegistry evidence for the skill does not attest the external repository. External evidence does not attest the skill. Audit cache reuse is allowed only when its subject tuple exactly matches the declared/effective state and snapshot digest; it does not bypass snapshot admission.\n\nA syntax-only offline check that cannot obtain an exact protected snapshot warns `build_repository_unverified_offline` and makes no source/audit/build claim. Install, update, repair, and coverage-claiming audit fail before mutation when the exact effective snapshot cannot be obtained and audited.\n\nDry-run may use network and removable operation-private fetch state, but it leaves no persistent repository, snapshot, audit response, lock, receipt, marker, or cache mutation. It must validate and audit the exact snapshot before reporting cache-hit or would-build.\n\n## 8. Receipt v2, cache identity, and mixed schema-7 builds\n\n### 8.1 Unsubstituted external receipt input\n\nReceipt-v2 input binds the complete source state:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 2,\n  \"driver\": \"go-repository-v1\",\n  \"source\": {\n    \"repository\": \"golden-tools\",\n    \"declared\": {\n      \"identity\": {\n        \"kind\": \"network-git\",\n        \"value\": \"github.com/example/golden-tools\"\n      },\n      \"transport\": \"https\",\n      \"locked_commit\": {\n        \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n        \"hex\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\"\n      },\n      \"tag\": \"v1.4.0\"\n    },\n    \"effective\": {\n      \"identity\": {\n        \"kind\": \"network-git\",\n        \"value\": \"github.com/example/golden-tools\"\n      },\n      \"transport\": \"https\",\n      \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n      \"commit\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\",\n      \"substituted\": false,\n      \"build_source\": {\n        \"algorithm\": \"curator-build-source-v1\",\n        \"content_sha256\": \"sha256:bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"descriptor\": {\n      \"path\": \"curator-build.json\",\n      \"target\": \"golden-tool\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"command\": \"golden-tool\",\n  \"build_root\": \".\",\n  \"source_dir\": \"cmd/golden-tool\",\n  \"target\": {\n    \"goos\": \"darwin\",\n    \"goarch\": \"arm64\",\n    \"tuning\": {\n      \"GOARM64\": \"v8.0\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"toolchain\": {\n    \"algorithm\": \"curator-go-toolchain-v1\",\n    \"go_relpath\": \"bin/go\",\n    \"go_version\": \"go version go1.26.1 darwin/arm64\",\n    \"content_sha256\": \"sha256:cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc\"\n  },\n  \"policy\": {\n    \"module_mode\": \"vendor\",\n    \"network\": \"none\",\n    \"workspace\": false,\n    \"cgo\": false,\n    \"compiler_directives\": \"reject-nonstandard-cgo-import-dynamic-v1\",\n    \"target_mode\": \"native\",\n    \"link_mode\": \"internal\",\n    \"libgcc\": \"none\",\n    \"package_assembly\": false,\n    \"host_objects\": false,\n    \"telemetry\": \"off-private\",\n    \"source_kind\": \"locked-external-git-v1\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 8.2 Substituted external receipt input\n\nOnly the source portion changes for a local substitution:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"repository\": \"golden-tools\",\n  \"declared\": {\n    \"identity\": {\n      \"kind\": \"network-git\",\n      \"value\": \"github.com/example/golden-tools\"\n    },\n    \"transport\": \"https\",\n    \"locked_commit\": {\n      \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n      \"hex\": \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567\"\n    },\n    \"tag\": \"v1.4.0\"\n  },\n  \"effective\": {\n    \"identity\": {\n      \"kind\": \"operator-local-git\",\n      \"value\": \"sha256:eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee\"\n    },\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"commit\": \"89abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\",\n    \"substituted\": true,\n    \"substitution\": {\n      \"type\": \"local-path\"\n    },\n    \"build_source\": {\n      \"algorithm\": \"curator-build-source-v1\",\n      \"content_sha256\": \"sha256:ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"descriptor\": {\n    \"path\": \"curator-build.json\",\n    \"target\": \"golden-tool\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nA network substitution instead uses `identity.kind: \"network-git\"`, its canonical value and transport, and `substitution: {\"type\":\"network-git\",\"ref\":<structured-ref>}`.\n\nThe complete receipt-v2 input is canonicalized with CCJ-1. Its SHA-256 is the artifact cache key. The key therefore cannot describe declared provenance while compiling substituted bytes.\n\nReceipt v2 retains exact canonical stored bytes, manager-derived artifact path, artifact SHA-256, and byte size. It has no trust/provenance boolean. Protected-state admission remains out of band.\n\nFor `effective.substituted: false`, the presence of `declared.tag` is a semantic\nreceipt precondition: the writer may emit and publish the receipt only after\nthat operation's exact-tag acquisition proves the tag terminates at\n`declared.locked_commit`. A self-asserted `tag_verified` boolean is not added;\nit would not prove the fetch. Receipt admission instead depends on the fixed\noperation ordering and protected snapshot/receipt boundary. A substituted\nreceipt records the manifest's declared tag only as declared state and makes no\nclaim that the remote tag was consulted while compiling substituted bytes.\n\n### 8.3 Mixed command behavior\n\nOne schema-7 installation may contain both command kinds:\n\n- local `go-v1` commands keep receipt v1 and the consuming skill's raw `build_source`;\n- external `go-repository-v1` commands use receipt v2 and per-command external source state;\n- the two drivers never share receipt interpretation or logical cache keys;\n- marker v3 represents both simultaneously;\n- top-level marker `build_source` is present exactly when at least one active local `go-v1` command exists and retains schema-6 meaning;\n- external-only installations omit top-level skill `build_source`; each external build entry carries its source identity and digest.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
